Normalisation

To keep the database clean and avoid duplicate data, the peak_university schema is structured up to Third Normal Form (3NF). 

1NF: Every column holds a single, indivisible piece of data with no repeating groups—for instance, splitting names into separate first and last name columns.

2NF:All non-key fields depend entirely on the primary key, avoiding partial dependencies (especially in our `grades` junction table which links students and courses).

3NF:There are no transitive dependencies. Information like department or course details are kept in their own dedicated tables rather than duplicated inside student records.
